# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Cache-Control is NOT set here. Pages serves its static assets with
# public, max-age=14400 and a _headers rule does not override that: on a
# fresh edge miss, /audio/index.json came back with the rule applied twice
# (Pages' own value for a .json matched ours, so both were appended) while
# /app/engine.js kept Pages' four hours and dropped ours entirely. Four
# hours is how two verified deploys never reached the browser.
#
# So caching is set in functions/_middleware.js, after the asset is served
# and where nothing overrides it. This file is left for headers Pages does
# not set itself.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
